// Title: DLL Execution Via Register-cimprovider.exe
// Sigma ID: a2910908-e86f-4687-aeba-76a5f996e652
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Ivan Dyachkov, Yulia Fomina, oscd.community
// Date: 2020-10-07 | Modified: 2021-11-27
// ATT&CK: privilege-escalation, persistence, execution, stealth, T1574
// Description: Detects using register-cimprovider.exe to execute arbitrary dll file.
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://twitter.com/PhilipTsukerman/status/992021361106268161
//   - https://lolbas-project.github.io/lolbas/Binaries/Register-cimprovider/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/adf5a626c4a776f3f023056f0f398b9523a2f09e/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_registry_cimprovider_dll_load.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where FolderPath endswith "\\register-cimprovider.exe" and (ProcessCommandLine contains "-path" and ProcessCommandLine contains "dll")
